<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rodulf, King of the Heruli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 508</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rodulf was king of the Heruli on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in the early 6th century. Around 507 the Ostrogothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a> adopted him as his son in arms, binding him to the Ostrogothic alliance. Around 508 he attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> under King Tato and was killed in a heavy defeat that broke Herul power north of the Danube.</p></div>
